  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1114 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nAbove mentioned front will bring a respite from the heat and\nhumidity for a couple of days, though points near the Red River\nmay still see HI in the 100-015 range Wednesday afternoon. Dew\npoints will lower into the 60s and high temps should trend near or\neven a bit below normal through Thursday. \n\nFront will begin to lose influence by Friday as low level flow\nreturns from the south. There are indications of a piece of\nshortwave energy topping the upper ridge with some increase in \nthunderstorm chances Thursday night and again Friday night as \nwell. Beyond that the ridge is forecast to expand back across the\nregion this weekend and early next week, beginning another \nstretch of hot weather and additional headlines. Should note that\nNBM forecast highs are likely a bit warm next week, but triple \ndigit heat appears likely in any case.",
